Atoms that tie on tier, conditions and cover are ordered by their rule
text, not by occurrence. An atom repeated in a later file is emitted once.

  $ cat > a.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_one", ["._one{a:b}"], 1, 0, 1, []);
  >   ("_two", ["._two{a:b}"], 1, 0, 1, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ cat > b.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_three", ["._three{a:b}"], 1, 0, 1, []);
  >   ("_two", ["._two{a:b}"], 1, 0, 1, []);
  >   ("_one", ["._one{a:b}"], 1, 0, 1, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ styled-ppx.generate a.ml b.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._one{a:b}
  ._three{a:b}
  ._two{a:b}
